  "abstract": "Stress-tests the cosmological viability of discrete entropic gravity with \u039b-locked screening by comparing three transition-scale scenarios against linear structure-formation observables. Only the \u039b-locked scenario (L_\u039b = 4.4 Gpc) preserves a realistic \u03c3\u2088 \u2248 0.8, while sub-Hubble transitions at 10 Mpc and 1 Mpc produce catastrophic overgrowth (\u03c3\u2088 >> 1). Establishes \u039b-locking (L_\u039b \u2273 H\u2080\u207b\u00b9) as a necessary condition for cosmological consistency.",
